# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
service-account*.json
gcp-*.json
# Whatever Google hands you keeps its download name, and neither form
# matches the two patterns above. A client_secret_*.json landed in this
# working tree on 2026-08-11 and was one `git add -A` from being public.
client_secret*.json
*apps.googleusercontent.com*.json
*-service-account*.json
# A service account key downloads as <project>-<hash>.json, which matches
# none of the patterns above. Ignore the whole shape, and any .json sitting
# loose in the repo root — nothing the project needs lives there.
/*.json
!package.json
!package-lock.json

# ── Real customer data — NEVER commit ───────────────────────────────────────
# This repository is public. Everything below contains either live credentials
# or personal data belonging to real customers, which makes committing it a
# breach under both Egyptian and Saudi PDPL, not merely untidy.
#
#   api_response.txt              live Bitrix REST token in deal_info_endpoint,
#                                 plus a customer's name and CRM contact id
#   fixtures/chats/*.json         same payload
#   fixtures/calls/*.wav          recordings of real customers' voices
#   docs/samples/*.json           verbatim transcripts and phone numbers
#   docs/call-evaluation.html     rendered transcript
#
# Keep them on local disk. See fixtures/README.md for how to populate them.
api_response.txt
fixtures/chats/
fixtures/calls/
docs/samples/
docs/call-evaluation.html
*.wav
*.mp3
*.ogg

# Internal design docs that quote the live payload
build-spec.html
customer-360-explained.html
schema-map.html
schema.html
final-erd.html
*.pdf
*.docx
# Conversation exports from Bitrix. `Conversation - Travelgate 7 & 8.xlsx` holds
# 72,869 real customer messages — 1,125 with phone numbers, 22 with emails.
*.xlsx

# The rendered customer archive — 375 KB of real customers, names and passport
# references. Same reason as everything above it.
TravelGate Customer Archive*.html

# Scored output from local test runs: transcripts, phone numbers, itineraries and
# agent names, as HTML reports and as the raw JSON behind them.
local-reports/

# ── Python ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ── Local scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
/tmp/
chunks/

# local Claude Code settings (contain secrets)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Bitrix CRM exports — real customer names, phone numbers and deal values.
# This repo is public (CLAUDE.md rule 7). The one-off phone backfill reads
# these from disk; they are never committed.
DEAL_*.csv
CONTACT_*.csv
